#
# Google style — the most widely adopted modern C++ style.
# Used by Chromium, TensorFlow, Abseil, Protobuf, gRPC, V8, and most
# Google-affiliated open-source C++ projects.
#
#   2-space indent, 80-col line limit, K&R braces, public:/private:
#   outdented by 1, sorted #includes, pointer-left ("int* p").
#
# Keep this file pure "BasedOnStyle: Google" with zero overrides so
# the indent that nvim inserts (also 2 via ~/.editorconfig) is exactly
# what clang-format produces — no whitespace churn on save.
#
# Per-project .clang-format in a repo root takes precedence over this one.

BasedOnStyle: Google
